U.S. Bureau of Mines. Design of Surface Mine Haulage Roads: A Manual, Information Circular 8758, 1977, 50 pages. [Official CDC/NIOSH archive and report](https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/8915).

Read the whole manual, including alignment, geometry, materials, cross slope, drainage, and operating context. Treat empirical/vehicle examples as dated cases and compare with actual current equipment data, geotechnical evidence, operating conditions, and engineering methods. A road grade or width needs its complete design basis.

Official identity, year, length, scope, and authorized archive checked on 29 October 2026. Preserve agency and third-party component notices. Historical technical guidance is distinguished from current requirements and from a completed real-road design. No manual or vehicle dataset is bundled.

